  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 205 AM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nMoisture will be scoured out Tuesday, with PWATs dropping down to \nnear to slightly below normal. This combined with less favorable \nthermodynamics and increasing subsidence aloft will translate to a \nnotable downtick in storms Tuesday afternoon, with only isolated \nactivity favoring the Southwest and South Central Mountains. \n\nThe monsoon ridge will then shift westward into The Great Basin \nWednesday and Thursday. A shortwave riding over the ridge will exit \ninto the High Plains Wednesday afternoon, sending a backdoor front \ninto eastern NM and replenishing moisture once again. The uptick \nThursday (and potentially Friday) will be relatively short-lived as \ndrier air sneaks back in from the southeast. \n\nThe other story mid to late week will be the heat. Temperatures will \ngenerally run 5 to 10 degrees above normal, which will create \npockets of major heat risk in lower elevation areas, including \nAlbuquerque and Roswell. Model consensus shows the ridge centering \nitself over the southern Rockies late week, with weak easterly \nsteering flow over most of New Mexico. The monsoon high is progged \nto slowly shift eastward late week into the weekend, with easterly \nflow becoming more southerly.",
